This is a backport of the RK3528 USB2PHY support that landed upstream in
v7.2-rc1 (after v7.1.x). The two original commits do not apply cleanly to
the v7.1.x phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c due to surrounding context drift, so
this single consolidated patch carries both changes and is generated
directly against v7.1.1:

  2775541de058 "phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: Add clkout_ctl_phy support"
  864b3617df82 "phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: Add support for RK3528"

The E20C USB host port depends on the rockchip,rk3528-usb2phy compatible
and clkout_ctl_phy handling; without it usb2phy never probes and the
EHCI/OHCI host controllers defer forever.

